  "note": "The reaction depth bound holds for a saga's compensation too. The Watch saga marks a lamp when it is lit, and that mark is compensable. Lamp.Flicker then triggers itself on every Flickered; the flicker the fifth reaction announces reaches the saga at the ceiling, so its leg is refused and the saga unwinds. The saga still unwinds: its refused leg moves it to unwound, and the compensation (Unmark) and the hand-written refused leg (Retire) are reactions at that depth, so they are logged undelivered (Unmark as compensation_failed) and refused as well: the Lit mark stays, no Unmarked, no LampRetired. The saga log is frozen so both runtimes are held to that unwind.",
